      "dom_id": "question-1477",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Simplify the statement $¬(P⇒Q).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that\n\n$$\n¬(P⇒Q)≡¬(¬P∨Q).\n$$\n\nWe can distribute the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n¬(¬P∨Q)≡¬(¬P)∧¬Q.\n$$\n\nFinally, canceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n¬(¬P)∧¬Q≡P∧¬Q.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $P∧¬Q.$",
