      "dom_id": "question-182498",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Simplify the statement $¬(R⇒¬S).$",
      "worked_solution": "The conditional statement $P⇒Q$ is logically equivalent to the disjunction $¬P∨Q:$\n\nSo, in this case, we have the following equivalence:\n\n$$\n¬(R⇒¬S)≡¬(¬R∨¬S)\n$$\n\nDistributing the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law, we have\n\n$$\n¬(¬R∨¬S)≡¬(¬R)∧¬(¬S).\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negation, we reach\n\n$$\nR∧S.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $R∧S.$",
