      "problem": "$\\,$ Wear a jacket, or you will get cold.\n\nWhich conditional statement is logically equivalent to the disjunctive statement above?",
      "worked_solution": "Let's denote by $A$ and $B$ the following statements:\n\n- $A:$ Wear a jacket.\n\n- $B:$ You will get cold.\n\nThen, our initial statement can be written as $A∨B,$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬A⇒B.\n$$\n\nThe negation of $A$ can be written as\n\n- $¬A:$ You don't wear a jacket.\n\nTherefore, the given statement is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ If you don't wear a jacket, then you will get cold.",
